# The build is byte-exact (see docs/ADR-001-source-split.md): a src/ fragment
# checked out with CRLF would silently add ~3,100 bytes to dist/fieldbook.html.
# Pin line endings so a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true cannot break it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.zip binary

# ---- parallel worktrees ----
# Several issues are worked at once, one worktree each, then merged back. These
# two files are append-only logs that EVERY branch adds to, so a plain 3-way
# merge conflicts on every single merge after the first — on lines that do not
# actually disagree. `union` keeps both sides.
src/docs/UNRELEASED.md            merge=union
src/docs/_claude/WIRING-LEDGER.md merge=union

# Safety net, and it should never fire: feature branches carry src-only diffs
# and never commit the artifact. If one does, keeping ours and rebuilding is the
# only sane resolution — a 473 KB generated file has no meaningful 3-way merge.
# Needs a driver definition, which scripts/wt.sh sets:
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
dist/fieldbook.html               merge=ours
